00:36:13,934 --> 00:36:15,968
was your issue resolved?

357
00:36:16,368 --> 00:36:17,568
thumbs up, thumbs down.

358
00:36:17,742 --> 00:36:23,008
Those would tell me how good is my prompt, and I can engineer that prompt, optimize it, and I would probably drive some gains.

359
00:36:23,568 --> 00:36:28,036
but I will not be able easily to trace back to what the problem was.

360
00:36:28,398 --> 00:36:35,168
While in the second approach, not only I can use the end-to-end metrics to improve my process, I can also use the intermediate steps.

361
00:36:35,328 --> 00:36:41,508
For example, if I look at prompt two and I look at the outline and I see the outline is actually meh, it's not great.

